#: includes/class-admin.php:339
msgid "In the Google Cloud Console, under the “Google Auth Platform” menu, follow these steps in order:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:341
msgid "Create / choose a project"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:342
msgid "Branding — set the app name and logo (what the user sees on the Google screen)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:343
msgid "Audience → Test users → add your own email (required for testing before publishing)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:344
msgid "Clients → Create client → type “Web application” → paste the Redirect URI (above)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:346
msgid "When the client is created (step 4), Google shows the Client ID and the Client Secret — paste them into the form on the left."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:351
msgid "In the Azure portal (Microsoft Entra ID), follow these steps in order:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:354
msgid "Register an application (opens the registration form directly)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:355
msgid "under “Name”, enter your store name: it is what customers see on the Microsoft consent screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:357
msgid "Under “Supported account types” choose “Personal Microsoft accounts only” (the last option in the list) — that is what covers Hotmail, Outlook.com and Live."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:358
msgid "Under “Redirect URI” select the “Web” platform and paste the Redirect URI (above). Click “Register”."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:359
msgid "You land on the app’s “Overview”: copy the “Application (client) ID” and paste it into the Client ID field on the left."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:360
msgid "In the app’s sidebar open “Certificates & secrets” → “New client secret” → choose the expiry (recommended: 730 days / 24 months, otherwise sign-in stops working when it expires) → “Add”."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:361
msgid "Copy the secret’s “Value” column (careful: NOT the “Secret ID”) — it is shown only once. That is the Client Secret; ideally define it in wp-config.php (constant shown below the field)."
msgstr ""

